# Xcode and Simulator: MCP only

**Scope:** Binding only when `dev-ios-scope.mdc` marks this workspace active (iOS Simulator workflow). When inactive, ignore this entire rule — use Shell `xcodebuild` on macOS.

## Simulator UI forbidden

Never open Simulator.app and never launch an app in the Simulator. Allowed XcodeBuildMCP tools are `build_sim` and `test_sim` only. `test_sim` runs unit tests with mocks. Do not call `boot_sim`, `open_sim`, `build_run_sim`, `install_app_sim`, `launch_app_sim`, `stop_app_sim`, `screenshot`, `snapshot_ui`, `tap`, `touch`, `long_press`, `swipe`, `drag`, `gesture`, `button`, `key_press`, `key_sequence`, `type_text`, `wait_for_ui`, `record_sim_video`, or `debug_attach_sim`. Do not run `serve-sim`, `swiftui-preview-browser.py`, `open -a Simulator`, `simctl boot`, or `simctl launch`. If a task needs the Simulator window, stop and say this plugin does not launch Simulator UI.

Build, test, launch, boot, and shutdown on **Simulator** go through **`XcodeBuildMCP` only**. Do not use the Shell tool (or any other non-MCP tool) for Simulator build/test/launch operations.

Never run, chain, or wrap any of these in Shell, including after `pkill`, `kill`, `nohup`, or `sleep`:

- `xcodebuild` (including `test-without-building`)
- `xcrun`, `simctl`, `xcode-select`
- `instruments`, `xed`, `agvtool`, `ibtool`, `actool`

**Reading logs and crashes is allowed.** Use Read, Grep, or Glob on runtime console logs, crash reports, and Diagnostics for the host app on Simulator or device, including paths under `~/Library/Logs/` (for example `CoreSimulator`, `DiagnosticReports`), `~/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Devices/…/data/Library/Logs/`, log paths under yaml `derivedDataPath` (`Logs/`, `.xcresult`), and log file paths returned by MCP (`test_sim`). `debug_attach_sim` does not replace those for a crash that already happened; read the on-disk logs when investigating a prior crash.

Do not **write** or **delete** under `DerivedData`, `SourcePackages`, `CoreSimulator`, `~/Library/Developer/Xcode`, `~/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator`, or `/Applications/Xcode.app` unless the user explicitly asks. Do not `kill` / `pkill` `xcodebuild` PIDs from `simulator-status.sh`.

If XcodeBuildMCP is unavailable, stop and report that. Do not fall back to Shell for build, test, launch, boot, or shutdown. The only Shell exceptions are bundled scripts under `plugins/dev-ios/skills/*/scripts/` when the matching skill is loaded and instructs that script — in particular `resolve-derived-data-path.sh` from `build-ios-apps`, `simulator-status.sh` from `ios-simulator-browser` (read-only inventory: `simctl list` and `pgrep`), and `simulator-shutdown.sh` from `ios-simulator-browser` (`simctl shutdown` only; no signals and no quit Simulator.app).
